# =============================================================================
# CMO Simulator — environment variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values for your project.
# Never commit .env.local to version control.
# =============================================================================

# Required — Supabase project URL and anon key (both are browser-safe)
# Self-hosted (Coolify) shared API URL example:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://supabase.darlingmartech.com
# Use the literal anon JWT string here. Next.js reads .env.local directly;
# placeholders like ${SERVICE_SUPABASEANON_KEY} only work if that name is also
# defined in the SAME file (or your host injects real env vars at runtime).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Required — used for absolute URL generation and auth redirects locally
# Local dev uses port 3002 (see package.json "dev" script).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3002

# Server-only — required for sign-up confirmation emails via Resend (see below).
# Do NOT prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — this must never be exposed to the browser.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
#
# Resend (transactional email for email confirmation on sign-up)
# Create an API key at https://resend.com/api-keys — "From" must be a verified sender/domain.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL="CMO Simulator <onboarding@yourdomain.com>"
# Optional reply-to (also accepts RESEND_TO_EMAIL as an alias used in some setups):
# RESEND_REPLY_TO=
#
# If RESEND_API_KEY, RESEND_FROM_EMAIL, and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are all set,
# the app sends confirmation links through Resend. Otherwise sign-up falls back to
# Supabase's built-in mail (configure SMTP in the Supabase dashboard for that path).
#
# Production (Vercel) example names only — set values in the dashboard, never commit:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://supabase.darlingmartech.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<Coolify SERVICE_SUPABASEANON_KEY>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://cmo-simulator-eight.vercel.app
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<Coolify SERVICE_SUPABASESERVICE_KEY>  # optional, server-only
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase Auth — allow-list for where users land after email links (PKCE callback)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard path (wording varies slightly by UI version):
#   Project (select yours) → left sidebar "Authentication" → "URL Configuration"
# There is NO top-level menu item named "Redirect URLs". On URL Configuration you will
# see "Site URL" plus a list/field labeled "Redirect URLs" (or "Additional Redirect URLs").
#
# Direct URL (replace YOUR_PROJECT_REF — from Project Settings → General → Reference ID):
#   https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/YOUR_PROJECT_REF/auth/url-configuration
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL must match the site users open (local vs production), because
# password reset emails use it to build links to /auth/update-password.
#
# On that page, add each line to the redirect allow list (wildcards like /** are ok):
#   http://localhost:3002/auth/callback
#   http://localhost:3002/auth/update-password
#   http://localhost:3002/**
#   https://cmo-simulator-eight.vercel.app/auth/callback
#   https://cmo-simulator-eight.vercel.app/auth/update-password
#   https://cmo-simulator-eight.vercel.app/**
#
# Site URL in Supabase can be the production app URL; local still works if redirect
# URLs include localhost as above.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Self-hosted Supabase (e.g. Coolify at supabase.example.com) — no URL UI in Studio
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hosted Studio often only exposes pieces like Authentication → Users. Full "URL
# Configuration" from supabase.com may not exist. That is normal: GoTrue reads env vars.
#
# In Coolify, open your Supabase stack and find the auth / gotrue service (name varies
# by template). Set the site + allow-list there, then redeploy/restart that service.
#
# Typical variable names (confirm against your stack’s compose / Coolify env docs):
#   GOTRUE_SITE_URL=https://your-cmo-simulator-app.example.com
#   GOTRUE_URI_ALLOW_LIST=http://localhost:3002/**,https://your-cmo-simulator-app.example.com/**
# Use comma-separated entries; globs like /** are supported (see GoTrue docs).
#
# Your app must pass redirect_to values that match this allow list (this repo uses
# e.g. https://.../auth/callback?next=... for email confirmation).
#
# Official reference: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/self-hosting/auth/config
#
# Optional: try whether your Studio exposes the page at all (may 404 on some builds):
#   https://supabase.darlingmartech.com/project/default/auth/url-configuration
